{"x":8,"y":2,"captures":[[{"rule":0,"flash":[],"flips":[]}]],"p1s":5,"p2s":5,"eb":0,"z":"red/75794f5d555e4848424f5f4a3178227e37342a74642f333f242569356d","u":1,"c":"42","dialog":[[{"buttons":[{"name":"Skip Tutorial","link":"0"},{"name":"Start Tutorial","direction":1}],"content":"<p>Welcome to the Elemental Tutorial.</p><p>Would you like to see a quick demonstration about how the rule works?</p>"},{"position":[50,"top"],"width":250,"buttons":[{"name":"Back","direction":-1},{"name":"Okay","direction":1}],"content":"<p>An Elemental game begins with various elemental properties scattered across open positions on the game board. You can see some behind me: that's Wind on the top, Fire in the center, and two Water elements.</p><p>Other's are Ice, Lightening, Poison, Earth and Light.</p>"},{"buttons":[{"name":"Back","direction":-1},{"name":"Okay","direction":1}],"content":"<p>Some of the cards also possess an elemental property. If played on a matching property on the board, then its ranks increase by 1, otherwise they decrease by 1.</p><p>Let's have look!</p>"}],[]],"gameover":[]}
{"x":1,"y":"0","captures":[[{"rule":0,"flash":[],"flips":[]}]],"p1s":5,"p2s":5,"eb":-1,"z":"Ymx1ZQ==/6d3c7451714f402d38405d3b3870353d6826797654544c2b3e38385f5c","u":2,"c":"7","dialog":[[],[{"buttons":[{"name":"Okay","direction":1}],"content":"<p>Blue just played onto a position which had the Wind elemental property. The card they played didn't also possess Wind. As a result, that card's ranks are all decreased by 1 for the remainder of the game.</p>"}]],"gameover":[]}
